NotesRegister lists technical notes as an engineering drawing register (a revision table): date, note number, topic, title and standard, with topic filter chips and the latest or next planned note in a larger panel beside it.

- Data: block `"type": "register"` (`assets/src/blocks/register.js`). `topics: ["Standards", …]` (chip order), `items: [{t, topic, std, date, link, featured, d}]`. `t` title, `topic` one of `topics`, `std` the standard it reads, `link` a page id (the title links to it), `d` one line shown only in the featured panel, `spot` (optional) a Spot name for the featured panel's vignette. An item without `date` shows a mono "Planned" status: never invent a date, and placeholders stay placeholders.
- Featured: the item with `featured: true`, else the first item of the first topic. Labelled "Latest" when it has a date, "Next planned" when not. It also stays in the register (its number in `flow`).
- Markup: the section's figure is a light Plate (`wPlate`, title block "Aquemi | Notes register") holding `.aq-notes-register` grid > `.aq-notes-register__filter` (a framed bar, `role="group"`, a mono "Filter:" caption `__fk`, `button.aq-notes-register__chip` with `aria-pressed` and `data-topic`, drawn as `[bracketed]` mono tags; "All" first, each with its count), a visually hidden `aria-live` count, `aside.aq-notes-register__feature` (mono `__flabel` strip, `h3.__ft`, `p.__fd`, one `.aq-tag`, a Spot vignette `__vig` > `.aq-spot.__spot`, `__go` "Applied on <page>"), `.aq-notes-register__reg` > `table.aq-notes-register__table` (rows `tr[data-topic]`, the title a `th scope="row"` whose link covers the row).
- Spot: `item.spot`, else the linked page's equipment (`REG_SPOT` in `register.js`: sys-monitoring analyzer, sys-storage storage-tank, sys-pw ro-skid …). No vignette when neither names a known Spot.
- Filtering is client-side: a chip hides the other rows (`hidden`) and shows every matching row even if folded; the fold button hides while a topic is chosen. "All" restores the fold.
- Desktop: the bracket chips across the top in one framed bar (pressed: `flow-tint`, `flow` brackets and underline); panel (300 px) left with a `flow` top rule and a dashed vignette frame, register right: every cell ruled in `line-strong`, uppercase mono column heads on `surface-sunken`, mono `ink-muted` meta, sans `ink` titles, `flow-tint` on hover. Phones: the chip bar scrolls sideways inside its own frame only (44 px targets), the panel stacks above with a smaller vignette, rows keep the register's rules: a ruled mono number column, then title, topic and status, and the standard in mono.
- Ground: the navy, with the register on a cream plate (`light`). Tokens only.
- Supports `fold: N` (first N rows under "All") and `fold_noun` ("Show all 24 notes"). Order items so the first topic leads.
- Not for documents a buyer receives (DocList) or for comparisons (CompareTable). In use on news.

## Motion

`motion.js`: the cream plate unrolls, the [chips] click in left to right, the featured panel is cut in from the top with its Spot printing in after, then the ruled rows are entered one by one (each wipes left to right inside the already-ruled table) and the featured row's flow number settles last. On phones the rows play when the table itself scrolls in. Filtering (`register.js`) uses GSAP Flip: rows that stay glide to their new places, rows that join fade in; without GSAP or under reduced motion they switch instantly.
